+    # ADDITIVE, DEFAULT-OFF correctness enforcement (2026-10-31, Vikunja #203 residual). The 2026-09-02 fix above
+    # closed the Hebbian write sites only. A grep of EVERY write to cp_connections.data found three more that move a
+    # synapse declared plastic=False / plastic_internal=False, plus one bookkeeping path that makes the mask itself
+    # stale: (i) homeostatic SYNAPTIC SCALING (sim/bridge.py ~12287) multiplies every weight by the per-neuron scale
+    # factor - gated only by the named gain, never by the mask (measured: a frozen 20.0 synapse moves to 5.0, delta
+    # 15.0, over 30 reads of a 6-neuron probe); (ii) structural-plasticity ELIMINATION (~11972) zeroes any weight
+    # below struct_plast_weight_threshold regardless of the mask (measured: a frozen 0.02 synapse is zeroed); (iii)
+    # the reward-modulation CLIP (~11990) clips every weight to [w_min,w_max] when no named gain array exists
+    # (measured: a frozen 100.0 weight is clipped to hebbian_max_weight, 1.0 in the probe config -> delta 99.0);
+    # (iv) the plastic mask is never remapped
+    # across a CSR-reordering rebuild nor compacted, because the remap helper reads the DEAD attribute
+    # `cp_plastic_mask` (never assigned anywhere in sim/) instead of the live `cp_synapse_plastic_mask` (measured:
+    # after set_pathway_weights(add_missing=True), 4 of the 14 declared (pre,post) pairs are labelled with the wrong
+    # plasticity). When this flag
+    # is True (or the env var BRAIN_ENFORCE_PLASTIC_MASK is set truthy, the umbrella), all four sites honour the mask;
+    # 0/False => every branch is skipped => byte-identical to the pre-2026-10-31 behavior. Verified both directions by
+    # tests/test_plastic_mask_beyond_hebbian.py (freeze over 30 reads on 6 seeds; flag-OFF SHA == the SHA of the
+    # genuine pre-fix code, recovered with `git archive` of the flag commit's parent).
+    enforce_plastic_mask_beyond_hebbian: bool = False
